          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चाक — cāk — \"a potter's wheel\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कुम्हार चाक पर मिट्टी के दीये बनाता है। Kumhār cāk par miṭṭī ke dīye banātā hai. The potter makes clay lamps on his wheel."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चाक (cāk) is a tadbhava, inherited from Sanskrit cakra, \"a wheel\" (CDIAL 4538). CDIAL gives the Hindi word as \"any kind of wheel\"; at the potter's it is his wheel."
            }
          ]
        },
